# --- Datasets ---
# Image datasets get large fast and don't belong in git history. Either
# host them elsewhere (Kaggle, Google Drive, Roboflow, Git LFS, a release
# asset) and document the link in the README, or keep a small sample
# committed for demo purposes and .gitignore the rest.
images/
labels/
dataset/
real_images/
real_labels/
real_dataset/

# --- Trained model weights ---
# Same reasoning as datasets -- these are large binaries. Consider
# publishing weights as a GitHub Release asset instead of committing them.
runs/
*.pt
*.onnx

# --- Debug/scratch output from this project's scripts ---
debug_crops/
debug_real/
